<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101590" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαίρ-ωμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything made round</i> or <i>globular</i>:
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>round weight</i>, in steelyards, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mech.</u>
				853b32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> pl.,
				<i>buttocks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.211
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.707
			</span></i>; sg. in <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> generally,
				<i>curve</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῳδιακοῦ κύκλου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					5.32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> dub. sens. in
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				659.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
